  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the rule runs, so I haven't seen any panel data or alerts yet.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has these main fields:\n- `timestamp`\n- `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-371c8b39 Web logs overview\" has four panels. They show total requests, requests over time, responses by status code, and average bytes by file extension. The link is http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-371c8b39-web-logs-overview-baf7b70cc342.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-371c8b39 5xx spike\" (id `d5008abb-4643-4fec-8dc0-2269bc97add4`) checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` have a `response.keyword` matching `5xx` within a 5-minute window. The rule is created disabled by default, so I enabled it so it can fire.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may fall outside the last 5 minutes. If so, the rule won't fire until fresh 5xx traffic arrives.",
